WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.857
A case is not finished when the antivirus says done.

2
00:00:03.857 --> 00:00:09.309
It is finished when the person who owns the computer confirms the problem is gone.

3
00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:14.295
In this demonstration I follow up two school cases with their stakeholders.

4
00:00:15.396 --> 00:00:18.770
The two cases waiting for confirmation.

5
00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:23.876
DC-1, the ransomware on the library PC, which IT re-imaged.

6
00:00:23.876 --> 00:00:30.972
DC-2, a potentially unwanted program on a computer lab PC, blocked before install.

7
00:00:32.072 --> 00:00:39.766
I call each stakeholder on the directory number and tell them, in plain words: what we found, what was done,

8
00:00:39.766 --> 00:00:41.334
and what they must do.

9
00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:52.448
For the librarian: we found ransomware on the library PC; IT rebuilt it and restored your files from last night's backup; please check that your files open.

10
00:00:52.448 --> 00:00:54.800
Then I ask: is everything normal?

11
00:00:55.899 --> 00:00:57.693
Here are their replies.

12
00:00:57.693 --> 00:01:01.981
Joy Santos confirms: the PC is back and her files open.

13
00:01:01.981 --> 00:01:08.451
The lab custodian says students still see a Free Converter window when they log in.

14
00:01:09.552 --> 00:01:14.160
Rule F1.4 tells me what to do with each reply.

15
00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:19.083
So DC-1 is closed, with who confirmed it and when.

16
00:01:19.083 --> 00:01:20.460
DC-2 is re-opened.

17
00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:29.561
The installer was blocked, but something is still running at login, so the host goes back for a re-check like on Day 8.

18
00:01:29.561 --> 00:01:34.532
Without the call, we would have closed a case that is not solved.

19
00:01:35.632 --> 00:01:36.580
Your turn.

20
00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:41.703
In the CTM Virtual Lab, choose Day 9 and Activity 9.1.

21
00:01:41.703 --> 00:01:43.221
Five bank cases.

22
00:01:43.221 --> 00:01:51.095
Find each stakeholder in the directory, read the replies, and decide the next step.

23
00:01:51.095 --> 00:01:53.941
One stakeholder never answers.

24
00:01:53.941 --> 00:01:55.743
Count the attempts.

